{"uid":"7a2c88b084b3eec3","name":"test_a_fail_verdict_is_normalised_to_rejected_without_a_single_reask","fullName":"tests.test_contract_ladder#test_a_fail_verdict_is_normalised_to_rejected_without_a_single_reask","historyId":"4adb777122e626a9e3909db860cb630e","time":{"start":1791946009810,"stop":1791946009827,"duration":17},"description":"GH #209 defect 2 (Half B). The reference run's own reply. `fail` is\n    not in `HAT_SCHEMAS[\"review\"]`'s two-word enum, so it used to cost\n    three attempts, three `contract.violation`s, one `contract.agent_fault`\n    and -- once Half A landed -- would have cost a PAUSE, which is strictly\n    worse than the rejection it plainly meant. It is now normalised ahead\n    of the ladder's own early-exit check, so it never enters\n    `enforce_contract` at all and becomes a real, fully-furnished\n    rejection in ONE runner call.","descriptionHtml":"<p>GH #209 defect 2 (Half B). The reference run's own reply. <code>fail</code> is<br />\nnot in <code>HAT_SCHEMAS[&quot;review&quot;]</code>'s two-word enum, so it used to cost<br />\nthree attempts, three <code>contract.violation</code>s, one <code>contract.agent_fault</code><br />\nand -- once Half A landed -- would have cost a PAUSE, which is strictly<br />\nworse than the rejection it plainly meant. It is now normalised ahead<br />\nof the ladder's own early-exit check, so it never enters<br />\n<code>enforce_contract</code> at all and becomes a real, fully-furnished<br />\nrejection in ONE runner call.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791946009794,"stop":1791946009799,"duration":5},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791946009794,"stop